WEBVTT

00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:41.666
[Snake] Stop.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.835
<i>[Wolf] I'll stop if you just explain it</i>
<i>to me, because I don't...</i>

00:00:43.919 --> 00:00:46.421
- [Snake] Would you please just drop it?
- All right, all right. Fine, fine, fine.

00:00:46.505 --> 00:00:48.297
Consider it dropped.
It's dropped. It's on the ground.

00:00:48.382 --> 00:00:49.257
Good.

00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:53.094
But, I mean, come on,
everybody loves birthdays.

00:00:53.178 --> 00:00:54.011
[groans]

00:00:54.096 --> 00:00:55.471
You got decorations,
you got balloons,

00:00:55.556 --> 00:00:56.806
you got parties and cake.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.767
Look. I don't need presents,
I don't want decorations,

00:00:59.852 --> 00:01:01.477
and I'm not a cake guy.

00:01:01.562 --> 00:01:03.646
Seriously, though,
you don't like cake?

00:01:03.731 --> 00:01:05.815
Name one food
better than cake.

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:06.983
Guinea pig.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.609
Again, with the guinea pig.

00:01:08.694 --> 00:01:11.988
[chuckles] I bet if I blindfolded you,
you wouldn't be able to tell

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:14.449
the difference between
a skunk and a guinea pig.

00:01:14.533 --> 00:01:15.616
Wrong.

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:18.953
Snakes have impeccable taste buds.
I can taste air.

00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:20.997
- Air?
- Yes. Air.

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:23.249
[lapping] Mmm.

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:24.375
Nice.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:26.627
I don't know.
They're a little, uh...

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:28.045
They're a little cute
for my taste.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:30.423
That's what makes them
so delicious.

00:01:30.507 --> 00:01:34.010
You're not just eating food,
you're eating pure goodness.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.678
It's not about the pig.

00:01:35.763 --> 00:01:38.890
It's about what it symbolizes
on a deeper level.

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:42.018
So, you can...
You can taste air?

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:43.895
- Ah. Forget about it.
- What else you got?

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:45.938
Wait, wait, wait.
Can you also hear color?

00:01:46.023 --> 00:01:47.315
- [laughing]
- All right, all right.

00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:48.441
- Can you see sound?
- Okay.

00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:50.359
'Cause we should really be
capitalizing on these skills.

00:01:50.444 --> 00:01:51.611
Okay, all right, fine.

00:01:51.695 --> 00:01:53.946
- Get it all out. Get it all out now.
- Okay, okay.

00:01:54.031 --> 00:01:55.281
[gags]

00:01:55.365 --> 00:01:57.033
Look at that. 4:00 p.m.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.619
Now I know the exact moment
our friendship died.

00:01:59.703 --> 00:02:01.579
[laughs]

00:02:01.663 --> 00:02:03.164
- Let's bounce.
- Yep.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.960
Tastes like, uh, you're gonna stick me
with the bill... again.

00:02:08.045 --> 00:02:09.837
- Well, it is my birthday.
- [patrons gasp, shudder]

00:02:09.922 --> 00:02:12.465
So, now you play the birthday card?
That's interesting.

00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:13.841
[laughs]

00:02:13.926 --> 00:02:16.010
Can we get a check, please,
when you get a chance?

00:02:16.929 --> 00:02:19.096
Hello?
Checkity-check-check.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.098
You know what?

00:02:21.183 --> 00:02:24.268
We're just gonna leave
the money right here, okay?

00:02:24.895 --> 00:02:26.687
You know the one good thing
about this place?

00:02:26.772 --> 00:02:28.898
- What?
- We never have to wait for a table.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.191
Well, isn't that every place?

00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:31.901
Hey, man. How you been?
I haven't seen you...

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:33.820
- Snake attack! [laughs]
- [patrons gasping]

00:02:33.904 --> 00:02:35.488
Oh! Mints.

00:02:35.572 --> 00:02:37.657
Sorry, folks.
I'm switching him to decaf.

00:02:37.741 --> 00:02:39.242
[laughs]

00:02:39.326 --> 00:02:41.327
- All right.
- [both] Let's do this.

00:02:41.954 --> 00:02:45.540
- [pedestrians screaming]
- [tires screeching]

00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:48.876
- [screaming continues]
- [crashing]

00:02:55.384 --> 00:02:56.425
Guinea pig, huh?

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:58.261
It's the Rolls Royce of rodents.

00:02:58.345 --> 00:03:00.972
Yeah, but it's still a rodent.
You know what I mean?

00:03:02.349 --> 00:03:04.684
- Don't mind us, just robbin' this place.
- [people screaming]

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:08.771
- [glass shattering]
- [alarm blaring]

00:03:15.696 --> 00:03:17.405
[tires squealing]

00:03:17.489 --> 00:03:21.158
- Whoo! Yeah! Go bad...
- Or go home.

00:03:21.243 --> 00:03:22.243
[both laughing]

00:03:22.327 --> 00:03:24.287
[engine revs]

00:03:26.874 --> 00:03:29.375
Hey, you. Get over here.

00:03:29.918 --> 00:03:31.377
Little bit closer.

00:03:32.296 --> 00:03:34.714
Oh, I know what it is.

00:03:34.798 --> 00:03:38.551
You're afraid.
Because I'm the big, bad wolf.

00:03:39.136 --> 00:03:42.179
<i>Well, I'm not surprised.</i>
<i>I am the villain in every story.</i>

00:03:42.264 --> 00:03:44.974
- Isn't that right, Mr. Snake?
- [laughs] Yep.

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:47.393
Say hello to Mr. Snake.

00:03:48.186 --> 00:03:50.187
<i>Serpentine, safecrackin' machine.</i>

00:03:50.272 --> 00:03:52.315
<i>Imagine Houdini, but with no arms.</i>

00:03:52.399 --> 00:03:55.735
<i>Kinda guy who'd tell ya the glass</i>
<i>is half empty, then steal it from ya.</i>

00:03:55.819 --> 00:03:59.655
He's also my best bud,
and today's his birthday!

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:00.865
Not relevant.

00:04:00.949 --> 00:04:03.200
He's a sweetheart.
You're a sweetheart.

00:04:03.285 --> 00:04:04.285
[siren wailing]

00:04:04.369 --> 00:04:05.745
Well, look who's here.

00:04:05.829 --> 00:04:06.954
Took 'em long enough.

00:04:12.544 --> 00:04:13.753
Watch this.

00:04:15.213 --> 00:04:17.506
Three... Two...

00:04:17.591 --> 00:04:18.633
One.

00:04:19.134 --> 00:04:21.719
And over here is Ms. Tarantula.

00:04:21.803 --> 00:04:25.556
<i>Our in-house hacker, pocket search engine,</i>
<i>our traveling tech wizard.</i>

00:04:25.641 --> 00:04:27.183
<i>We call her "Webs."</i>

00:04:31.772 --> 00:04:33.356
- [siren blaring]
- [horns honking]

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:36.150
- Very slick, Webs.
- I also took over the police dispatch,

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:38.903
blurred their satellite imaging system,
grounded their chopper,

00:04:38.987 --> 00:04:40.821
and one more thing...

00:04:40.906 --> 00:04:42.031
You didn't.

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.741
I got a special delivery for...

00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:47.036
[screams] Whoa, don't eat me!
Please, don't eat me!

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.830
Happy birthday,
Mr. Grumpypants.

00:04:49.915 --> 00:04:51.540
I think I hate you.

00:05:01.551 --> 00:05:02.677
- Ooh!
- Oh!

00:05:05.555 --> 00:05:07.056
Guys! It's me!

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.474
I was the construction worker!

00:05:08.558 --> 00:05:12.353
[Wolf]
<i>And this is Mr. Shark, master of disguise.</i>

00:05:12.437 --> 00:05:15.022
<i>Apex predator of a thousand faces.</i>

00:05:15.899 --> 00:05:17.191
<i>His greatest trick?</i>

00:05:17.275 --> 00:05:20.820
Stealing the Mona Lisa,
<i>disguised as the Mona Lisa.</i>

00:05:20.904 --> 00:05:22.071
Dig that.

00:05:22.155 --> 00:05:24.949
Watch it, big tuna.
I'm tryin' to work here.

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:28.160
Keep it cool, baby.
Birthdays should be chill.

00:05:29.121 --> 00:05:31.622
<i>[Wolf] And rounding out the crew...</i>

00:05:31.707 --> 00:05:33.165
[knocking]

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:36.002
Surprise! [cackling]

00:05:36.086 --> 00:05:38.337
<i>[Wolf] ...is Mr. Piranha.</i>

00:05:38.422 --> 00:05:40.631
<i>- He's a loose cannon with a short fuse...</i>
- [thugs laughing]

00:05:40.716 --> 00:05:42.842
<i>...willing to scrap with anyone or anything.</i>

00:05:42.926 --> 00:05:44.093
<i>He's brave.</i>

00:05:45.095 --> 00:05:46.929
<i>- He's fearless.</i>
- [thugs screaming]

00:05:47.014 --> 00:05:49.098
<i>Uh, who am I kidding? He's crazy.</i>

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:52.268
[laughing, speaking Spanish]

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:55.563
Uh, Piranha,
did we forget something?

00:05:55.647 --> 00:05:58.274
- What?
- The present. You know?

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:00.860
Oh, um, of course I didn't forget.

00:06:00.944 --> 00:06:02.236
[siren wailing continues]

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:03.946
You know you fart
when you lie, right?

00:06:04.031 --> 00:06:05.740
What? No, I fart when I'm nervous.

00:06:05.824 --> 00:06:07.867
- Yeah. Nervous about lying.
- [stomach gurgling]

00:06:07.951 --> 00:06:08.951
I'm sorry.

00:06:09.036 --> 00:06:10.786
- [farts]
- [Tarantula] Piranha!

00:06:10.871 --> 00:06:13.706
- Don't breathe it in. I breathed it in!
- [Wolf, Snake gasp]

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:16.042
<i>[Wolf] Yeah, they're a bit eccentric,</i>
<i>but when you're born us,</i>

00:06:16.126 --> 00:06:18.753
<i>you don't exactly win</i>
<i>many popularity contests.</i>

00:06:18.837 --> 00:06:19.837
Shark!

00:06:19.921 --> 00:06:21.338
- [beachgoer] A shark!
- [screaming]

00:06:21.423 --> 00:06:23.841
Do I wish people
didn't see us as monsters?

00:06:23.925 --> 00:06:25.134
Eight legs, eight times the cardio!

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:27.094
- Spider!
<i>- [Wolf] Sure, I do.</i>

00:06:27.179 --> 00:06:28.220
What's up, papa?

00:06:28.305 --> 00:06:30.931
But these are the cards we've been dealt,
so we might as well play them.

00:06:31.016 --> 00:06:32.558
- [lock clicks]
- Jackpot!

00:06:32.642 --> 00:06:33.642
Yes!

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:37.271
[tires screeching]

